  "npm test -- --test-name-pattern \"an indented heredoc terminator in a plain shell script is not a terminator\"",project,pi-agent,"2026-08-31T12:33:06.363Z",local_mutation,fix/index-unquoted-scalar-assignments
  "npm test -- --test-name-pattern \"run-block content is dedented the way YAML delivers it to bash\"",project,pi-agent,"2026-08-31T12:33:06.363Z",local_mutation,fix/index-unquoted-scalar-assignments
  "npm test -- --test-name-pattern \"run-block dedenting refuses shapes YAML would not deliver as blocks\"",project,pi-agent,"2026-08-31T12:33:06.363Z",local_mutation,fix/index-unquoted-scalar-assignments
close_reason: "Confirmed by reading the path and by measurement: no dedent exists between publishInvocationsIn and shellScalars, the heredoc terminator is the single whitespace-sensitive rule, and a realistic run-block fixture measured failures 0 (clean over an unattested publish) before the fix and failures 1 after. Fixed with dedentRunBlocks applied to workflow-path sources only."
body: "CodeRabbit, Security & Privacy / Minor, scripts/shell-command-scan.ts:634-637 (PR 84):\n\n\"**Normalize YAML block-scalar indentation before scanning.** — `publishInvocationsIn` passes workflow text directly to `shellScalars`, which only removes leading tabs for `<<-`. YAML indentation remains in the source text, so a valid heredoc terminator can remain active in the scanner. The scanner then skips later assignments and can miss a variable-based publish.\n\nNormalize workflow block indentation before scanning. Add an audit regression with an indented terminator, `NPM=npm`, and \\$NPM publish after it.\"\n\nCodeRabbit's follow-up: \"The YAML indentation check should confirm the exact input passed to `shellScalars`. If indentation remains, the assignment rule must accept the YAML block indentation without accepting non-standalone shell syntax.\""
